{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126283-conotoxin-coated-relic-help-how-would-you-write-up-this-poison-and-increase-it-s-lethality-over-sessions","id":1126283,"title":"Conotoxin coated relic help. How would you write-up this poison and increase it's lethality over sessions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T06:36:01-07:00","id":1126283,"title":"Conotoxin coated relic help. How would you write-up this poison and increase it's lethality over sessions?","content":"I am wanting to have a relic weapon have a permanent coating of conotoxin (from one of the more dangerous cone snail species) upon it due to the scion being the child of a water deity and having a seashell collection. I also thought cone snail venom would be a good idea since poisoning by one is relatively rare and there are no anti-venom for treatment. Eventually I hope since I am using Scion 2.0 rules to have the relic grow more powerful (a part of which would include increasing the lethality of the venom). However I have never written-up a poison before and was wondering if anyone here could help me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","user":"Manannansun","date":". 08-08-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T16:04:03-07:00","id":1126491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126283-conotoxin-coated-relic-help-how-would-you-write-up-this-poison-and-increase-it-s-lethality-over-sessions#post1126283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wanting to have a relic weapon have a permanent coating of conotoxin (from one of the more dangerous cone snail species) upon it due to the scion being the child of a water deity and having a seashell collection. I also thought cone snail venom would be a good idea since poisoning by one is relatively rare and there are no anti-venom for treatment. Eventually I hope since I am using Scion 2.0 rules to have the relic grow more powerful (a part of which would include increasing the lethality of the venom). However I have never written-up a poison before and was wondering if anyone here could help me?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are using the Scion 2.0 rules, you can check out the section on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/hazards\" target=\"_blank\">Hazards</a>. Hazards can represent anything from a raging fire, to an injected toxin, to holding an object that is ripping the soul out of you. <br /> <br /> You will want to work with your Storyteller to work out the exact mechanics of conotoxin using the Hazard system, and then work out how many Dots it will cost to have that as a permanent feature of the weapon. I can see it potentially being exceptionally powerful, sort of like an extra attack, but I think it can be balanced out rather well. My big suggestion is to keep the toxin as Lethal, and not allow it to be Cumulative. It being Cumulative would be insanely powerful, and keeping it Lethal will just help balance things out a bit more.<br /> <br /> The challenge with balancing a poison is that it is essentially like taking an extra attack. I would suggest to not to add any Epic Attributes to the damage of the poison simply because that can really start pumping out horrific numbers. If you want to make balancing it out easier, I'd suggest giving it an activation cost, it will help bring it in line with some other things in the game. If your Storyteller gets anxious about the power making the weapon out-shine the other combat players, you could have the actual attack from the weapon deal no damage, only administer the poison. That way it doesn't start being an effective second attack. (or fourth attack if you double attack)<br /> <br /> If you want to 'level up' the effect, I'd suggest bumping the difficulty to resist the attack. It won't be too hard to math-out the exact effects of the poison. The numbers your Storyteller will need to look at are the average rolls to resist the effect (probably Stamina + Fortitude. Treat each dice as a 0.5 Success to work out the average roll) and the average Soak DV of people. However, if you want more magical ways to upgrade the poison, you could do something like have the poison taint the blood of the person poisoned by it, potentially poisoning people who try to help them. You could have it start functioning like a sickness, and start chaining to each person who as much as touches the poisoned person. Have an individual effected by it taint the very land around them and kill off plant and animal life, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}